IPSC IT Fest 2026: a zero-dependency static site generator

The site for an inter-school IT fest at The Doon School, 8 to 10 December 2026,
covering eight events. `node build.mjs` renders eighteen pages into ./site from
one data file and one stylesheet, with no dependencies at all.

Why a generator rather than nineteen hand-written files: every page shares a
rail, a bar, a drawer, a footer and a command palette, and every fact comes
from one place. Hand-editing nineteen copies of that chrome is how a site
drifts out of sync with itself before it ever ships.

Assets are fingerprinted with a content hash because school and institutional
hosting caches stylesheets hard, and without that a redeploy ships new markup
against last week's CSS. That is a real failure that happens to real school
sites, and it costs one line of build code to prevent.

Note PUBLISHING.md: the data file contains the real names, biographies and
letters of about two dozen students, most of them minors, so this repository is
private and must have that data replaced with fictional entries before it is
ever made public. The generator is the part worth showing; the roster is not
mine to publish.

The rendered ./site is gitignored: it is a build artifact, and the generator
plus the data file are the source of truth.

